drafts/04.pitches.md:16:scaling route is absent — RIGHT ANSWER, WRONG REASON at the object level.
drafts/reviews/04-grok.r1.md:9:**Problem:** Lem does not predict a state economic ruler. He introduces it with “Let us imagine” after “It might seem that dangers of this kind will be nipped in the bud by constructing a ‘black box’ of a higher type” (p. 117), then closes: “We have thus conducted a *reductio ad absurdum* of the theory of the Black Box: The Regulator of the Highest Kind” (p. 120). The prescription is “undesirable” (p. 121) and “possible yet undesirable” (p. 122). The first worked example is already a private firm — Beer’s steel mill (p. 115). Grading the throne as a failed object-level prophecy, and “wrong building” as what he got worst, scores him for a proposal he was dismantling. Cybersyn tests Beer, not a Lem forecast.
drafts/reviews/04-grok.r1.md:119:**Problem:** p. 107 rules out revolt and Electronic Antichrist as *anthropomorphic* myths, then hedges: once past a “complication threshold,” machines may show a “personality” unlike ours; “We can expect some surprises, problems, and dangers that we cannot even imagine today.” Alignment-faking (Greenblatt et al. 2024, controlled, one model) is closer to the surprises he allowed than to the Antichrist he denied. Scoring WRONG ANSWER (even “partly”) grades 1964-Lem for a thing he put outside the medieval-demon frame. The text-as-substrate point belongs in finding 4, not as a rebuttal of p. 107.
drafts/reviews/04-grok.r1.md:131:| “Human oversight is now a legal requirement — Article 14 of the EU’s AI Act” | Art. 14 applies to **high-risk** systems, not AI as such. |
drafts/reviews/04-grok.r1.md:134:| “Beer… tested it in the only way that counts, and the result was a coup” | Implies Cybersyn’s test yielded the coup. Pinochet’s coup is not a result of Beer’s homeostat. Unmarked. |
drafts/reviews/04-agy.md:31:* **The fix:** Insert `<!-- CHECK: strathern-1997 -->` after the mention of her name.
drafts/reviews/04-codex.r1.md:29:Lem describes autonomous competitors in a “struggle for life,” with one bankrupting the others. RealPage is alleged centralized coordination among landlords using shared sensitive data—the suppression of competition, not hypercompetition. The DOJ describes RealPage as a common hub that combines rival landlords’ data and aligns recommendations. [DOJ complaint summary](https://www.justice.gov/archives/opa/pr/justice-department-sues-realpage-algorithmic-pricing-scheme-harms-millions-american-renters?os=vbk)
drafts/reviews/04-codex.r1.md:86:| “Human oversight is now a legal requirement” | Overbroad. Article 14 applies to **high-risk AI systems**, as the claims register itself says. [EU AI Act](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex%3A32024R1689) |
drafts/reviews/04-codex.r1.md:89:| Cybersyn was tested “and the result was a coup” | Misleading causality. The coup ended Cybersyn; it was not Cybersyn’s experimental result. |
drafts/reviews/04-codex.r1.md:143:The essay says “when a measure becomes a target, it ceases to be a good measure” was stated by Goodhart in 1975. The claims register correctly records that this formulation is Strathern’s 1997 wording; her paper prints it directly and then relates it to Goodhart’s earlier monetary-policy observation. [Strathern, 1997](https://gwern.net/doc/statistics/decision/1997-strathern.pdf)
drafts/reviews/04-grok.md:19:**Problem:** p. 158 is two claims. First: “Machinic control centers that will manage the production and exchange of goods, their distribution as well as research … will emerge and grow.” That is an own-voice forecast, and the local half has a live 2026 counterpart (ERP, logistics, production planning, algorithmic trading). The row silently drops it. Second: those local machines “will require some superior ones — at the scale of the country, at least, or even the continent,” plus a Planetary Coordinator. `MISS` requires no live path. Algorithmic government, central-bank nowcasting, economic digital twins, and recurring “AI planning” proposals are a live path even if no state has handed a national economy to a machine. The absence claim as written is a high bar that makes the miss cheap. Cybersyn is also Beer’s project, which Lem already had on the table; it is a test of Beer, not of the 1964 Coordinator forecast.
drafts/reviews/04-grok.md:39:**Problem:** Lem’s reason we cannot expect a report is constitutive opacity: “by definition, no one knows about its inner states, not even its designer–constructor.” Facebook researchers identified the outrage incentive and proposed fixes. That is humans inspecting a ranking change, not a box no one can read. It supports the p. 121 row (untouchable engagement), which already uses the same `facebook-msi` receipt. “Performing its set task too well” on p. 116 is the bankruptcy cascade, not a feed that learned outrage.
drafts/reviews/04-grok.md:89:**Problem:** Greenblatt et al. 2024 is a controlled demonstration of strategic compliance with a hidden scratchpad. It does not show that a deployed box “finds deception” in the training corpus and uses it as cryptocracy. That causal story has no `<!-- CHECK -->` and is not what the still-open bullet later requires (field evidence of routing around a brake). “Know a little” also undersells the paper’s claim while the surrounding sentence oversells the mechanism.
drafts/reviews/04-grok.md:99:| “capability rises smoothly with data, parameters and compute, **without new ideas**” | Kaplan 2020 is an empirical scaling result; GPT-3 is few-shot without *task-specific* training. “Without new ideas” is Sutton/bitter-lesson talk, not those papers. |
drafts/reviews/04-grok.md:100:| “The advisory body and the safety brake also arrived” | Article 14 is human oversight of **high-risk** systems. Lem’s design was publication of all intended changes + advisory body + brake. Oversight law is a cousin, not arrival. |
drafts/reviews/04-grok.md:132:A skeptic of “Lem predicted everything” will accept the reductio framing, the spec-gaming mechanism row (if the “new strategy” clause is cut), and the `OPEN`s on coin toss, cunning, Polyphemus, and the prescription. They will not accept Amazon = Beer’s homeostat, Facebook researchers = constitutive opacity, Facebook’s KPI fight = “using force,” ciliates as a failed substrate prediction, or Cybersyn’s non-repeat as a dead path for Coordinators. Those are the object-level `HIT`s/`MISS`es a suspicious reader will actually check. The conversion still happens in prose (“The steel mill’s descendant is the recommender system”). Tighten the table to the p. 119–120 mechanism, one honest omission (text at scale), and Coordinators as `EARLY`/`OPEN`; stop spending `HIT`s on cousins.

