The decisive missed issue is time-sensitive: the essay says Article 14 human oversight “is now a legal requirement,” but EU Regulation 2026/1744 postponed the relevant high-risk obligations to December 2027/August 2028. That makes the claim register’s checked row stale, not merely rhetorically loose.
